IBM Plex — SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
=============================================

The font files in this directory are subsets of IBM Plex, redistributed
under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. They are bundled so CORE Takeoff
renders identically on a field-office machine with no internet access.

Files
-----
  ibm-plex-sans-latin.woff2      IBM Plex Sans, latin subset, VARIABLE
                                 (wght axis; serves the 400/500/600 the UI
                                 asks for from one file)
  ibm-plex-mono-latin-400.woff2  IBM Plex Mono Regular, latin subset
  ibm-plex-mono-latin-500.woff2  IBM Plex Mono Medium, latin subset

Provenance
----------
  Retrieved 2026-08-31 from Google Fonts' own `latin` subset builds
  (fonts.gstatic.com/s/ibmplexsans/v23/, .../ibmplexmono/v20/), the same
  files the redesign mocks loaded over the network. Unchanged bytes; only
  the `latin` unicode-range was kept (no cyrillic / greek / vietnamese /
  latin-ext), which is why the three files total 75,308 bytes.

  Copyright 2017 IBM Corp. All rights reserved.
  Upstream project: https://github.com/IBM/plex
  Reserved Font Name: none declared by IBM for Plex.

License text
------------
The full SIL Open Font License 1.1 governs these files. It is reproduced
verbatim upstream at:

  https://github.com/IBM/plex/blob/master/LICENSE.txt
  https://openfontlicense.org/

Summary of the obligations that apply to this repository, in plain terms
(the license text above is what actually binds, not this summary):

  - The fonts may be used, studied, modified and redistributed freely,
    including bundled with software, and including commercially.
  - They may not be sold on their own.
  - This notice and the license must travel with the font files.
  - Modified versions may not use the "IBM Plex" name without permission.

Nothing in this directory is loaded from a third-party host at runtime.
webui/tokens.css declares the @font-face rules against these local paths
and ends every stack in a system fallback (Segoe UI / Consolas), so a
blocked or missing file degrades rather than breaks.
